WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:07.658
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, the Harmonic Conjugate governs projective division along central lines.

2
00:00:07.658 --> 00:00:16.770
Four collinear points A, B, C, and D form a harmonic range when C and D divide segment A B internally and externally in the exact same ratio.

3
00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:33.080
Because the Centroid X two divides the segment from Circumcenter X three to Orthocenter X four in a one-to-two ratio, and the Nine-Point Center X five bisects X three X four, the four classical Euler centers X two, X four, X three, and X five form a canonical harmonic range with cross-ratio negative one.

4
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:48.420
Harmonic division recurs across Collection One: on the Feuerbach line, the Feuerbach point X eleven and its harmonic conjugate X twelve divide the ইনcenter X one and Nine-Point Center X five internally and externally in the ratio of their radii.
